ISO-10303-21;
/* Le032: \X2\…\X0\ escape spanning a physical CR LF line break; ISO 10303-21 §5.2: whitespace (including CR LF) within a string literal is ignored by the lexer, permitting a hex run to span a line boundary; broken pretty-printers or line-length limiters split \X2\30A2 30A4\X0\ with an actual CR LF between the two 4-digit groups; byte-greedy implementations consume the directive byte-by-byte and fail when they encounter CR (0x0D) inside the hex run; tolerant lexer must skip embedded whitespace inside \X2\ hex runs; GEOMETRIC_CURVE_SET IS model entity — OCC yields empty */
